// The return-position half of the interaction-boundary narrowing, kept in its
// own file because it recovers badly (see `ridl-diag-showcase/NOTES`, "a
// rejected return type reports the wrong thing and cascades"): the parser
// reports `expected a return type`, which says nothing about what is allowed,
// and then reads the rest of the member as an attribute block.
//
// One member per file section would be cleaner still, but the cascade is part
// of what is being recorded — a reader of the diagnostics snapshot should see
// what this actually looks like at a desk.

package diag.ridl

interface NarrowingReturns {

  /// Collection in return position.
  query listLevels(): [Level; 0..8]
}
